    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **51 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp37Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a derived `telephoneDisplay` field that formats the stored E.164 telephone for humans while leaving raw `telephone` untouched.\n\n**How it fits the existing design:** derived read-only Owner fields (e.g. `checkDigit`, `identityKey`) are declared in the OpenAPI spec \u2014 which generates `OwnerDto` at build time \u2014 and populated by MapStruct auto-mapping from `@Transient` getters on the `Owner` model. I followed that same pattern rather than adding a custom mapper expression.\n\n**Two edits:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` property (readonly string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getTelephoneDisplay()` that splits the stored E.164 number into country code + national digits (longest-match against the `+61`/`+1` codes the app already recognises, with a single-digit fallback), then renders `+<code> <national digits grouped in threes>`. So `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. `null` stays `null`; non-E.164 values are returned unchanged, so it never throws for seed/NANP data read back by other tests.\n\n`telephone` itself is never modified \u2014 it remains the raw E.164 value produced by the controller's existing `normalizeTelephone`.",
